# Site-local topology for luxmark — copy to `Makefile.local` (gitignored) and fill in.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS: the committed Makefile is environment-agnostic by fleet standard
# (`luxarch --doc FLEET-BUILD-DEPLOY-STANDARD`, "Per-repo Makefile convention"). A registry host is
# internal **topology** — not a secret, but a disclosure risk in a PUBLIC repo like this one — so it
# stays out of git while the Makefile itself is always committed. That split is what lets a clean
# clone run `make lint` / `make arch` with zero config: every recipe references the variable.
#
# Secrets never live here either. Credentials go in SOPS-encrypted files or a node-only `.env`,
# never in a Makefile, public repo or private.

# The private registry serving the fleet guard images and the internal copy of this app's image.
LUX_REGISTRY := registry.example.internal:5000

# Optional — defaults to LUX_REGISTRY. Set only if the app image lives somewhere else.
# LOCAL_REGISTRY := registry.example.internal:5000

# The prod node, reached through the OVH jump host (same box as www and luxof.life), and where the
# luxmark stack lives on it. Used by `make prod-*`.
PROD_JUMP := jump.example.com
PROD_NODE := 10.0.0.1
PROD_DIR  := /opt/luxardolabs/luxmark

# Where a dev stack (`make dev-deploy`, which pins .env.dev and runs compose locally) is reachable,
# for the smoke probe it ends with. Unset, `make smoke` refuses to run.
# SMOKE_URL := http://127.0.0.1:8080
